      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I would love to have this, but it is worth it to implement as there are some glaring issues:\n\n- Offering a higher quality audio channel would not prevent people from just using it to get higher quality voices. This would take a higher toll on servers from the required higher bandwidth;\n\n- As @{60651324fbe2815d2b9ff6cb|full_name} mentioned, most people would not use it at first, but I think this won't be a problem later down the line as people learn to use it from word-of-mouth, otherwise they will keep getting muted;\n\n- How feasible is this actually? I've never personally seen a game that offers multiple audio inputs from a single user, however I could be wrong;\n\n- It might be a bit annoying, but it doesn't take much to select the player blasting music and lowering down their volume to 5%, this way it automatically gets reset when you relaunch VRChat.\n\nNevertheless, solving these issues would result in a useful system where people's music is automatically muted for those who want it so, but not their voice. Which would allow for communication.\n\nHowever, IMO, this system would be much more beneficial in worlds with video players/background music for people that play VRChat with their own background music.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-11-10T00:21:15.459Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "With the rise in prominence of people blasting music through their mic, could we please get a secondary voice channel for users doing so?\n\nMaking that feature opt-in as well , so only those who want to hear it will would be a great idea IMO\n\n It is actually becoming an annoying issue. I find a bunch of people in every public instance blaring random music so I feel this has become relevant\n\nOne way to encourage people to use this would be to offer people a more stable and higher quality second channel for music\n\nMy reasoning for this is I don't want to have to mute people to not hear music, and if people were drawn to this then I wouldn't have to mute them in the first place, as I wouldn't hear the music in the first place.\n\nFinally, one more thing, there has been a rise of dummy accounts used as \"music bots.....\" It has been that wide spread. So having a way to clear up comms would be much appreciated",
